WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:04.700
Now the list I most want you to know cold, and not only for the exam.

2
00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:11.450
Rule thirty-seven says a vessel in distress, needing help, uses the signals in Annex four.

3
00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:13.775
Follow the list on screen.

4
00:00:14.025 --> 00:00:18.275
A gun or other explosive signal, fired about once a minute.

5
00:00:18.525 --> 00:00:22.500
A continuous sounding of any fog-signal apparatus.

6
00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:24.725
Your horn, held down.

7
00:00:24.975 --> 00:00:30.300
Rockets or shells throwing red stars, fired one at a time at short intervals.

8
00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:35.950
The signal SOS, by any method, and the spoken word Mayday by radio.

9
00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:43.475
The code flags November over Charlie, or a square flag with a ball, or anything like a ball, above or below it.

10
00:00:43.725 --> 00:00:49.225
Flames on the vessel, a red parachute flare or red hand flare, and orange smoke.

11
00:00:49.475 --> 00:00:54.525
Slowly and repeatedly raising and lowering your arms, outstretched to each side.

12
00:00:54.775 --> 00:00:57.150
That one needs no equipment at all.

13
00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:04.250
And the modern ones: a digital selective calling distress alert, an EPIRB signal, and a dye marker.

14
00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:07.025
Look for the pattern.

15
00:01:07.275 --> 00:01:09.150
Red and orange.

16
00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:11.200
Continuous sound.

17
00:01:11.450 --> 00:01:14.500
And anything that says Mayday or SOS.
